{%- comment -%}
  AJ Tee Archive — the binder. Every tee that has held the weekly slot, in
  pockets, with the week it ran printed on it.

  THE SET IS THE PRODUCT HERE. A page listing past features is a changelog and
  nobody reads it. A page showing a part-filled binder is an invitation to come
  back, which is the only reason a weekly section is worth running at all — and
  it makes the number on the homepage card mean something, because the numbers
  have somewhere to live.

  EMPTY POCKETS ARE DELIBERATE. A binder with three blanks at the end reads as a
  set in progress; the same binder cropped to its filled pockets reads as
  finished. They cost nothing and they are the whole difference between "here is
  what we did" and "here is what is coming".

  MINI SLABS, NOT THE HOMEPAGE CARD SHRUNK. The homepage card carries a grading
  label, a barcode, a serial, four stats and a sticker. At a third the width
  none of that is legible, and illegible detail reads as noise rather than as
  richness. This keeps the three things that survive the size — the sleeve, the
  week number, the name plate — and drops the rest.

  THE WEEK NUMBER COMES OFF THE PRODUCT, and falls back to position when it is
  absent. The agent writes `tee.week` when it promotes a tee. Counting backwards
  from today instead would be right until the first week the queue runs dry, and
  then every card behind the gap would be permanently mislabelled.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  # LIQUID DOES NOT ALLOW A FILTER INSIDE A BRACKET LOOKUP — written as
  # `collections[handle | default: 'tee-past']` this resolves to nil and the
  # section renders nothing, silently. Resolve the handle first.
  assign archive_handle = s.archive_handle | default: 'tee-past'
  assign archive = collections[archive_handle]
  assign filled = archive.products | size
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  THE BINDER READS IN WEEK ORDER, AND IT HAS TO BE SORTED HERE.

  Fixed 25 Aug 2026. The section took `archive.products` in whatever order the
  collection was sorted, which is alphabetical by title — so the binder read
  "Adopt a Familiar, Cartoon Network, Ric Flair" and the week numbers printed on
  the cards ran 002, 001, 003. A numbered archive in the wrong order is worse
  than an unnumbered one: it looks like the numbers are wrong rather than the
  sequence.

  WHY NOT JUST SET THE COLLECTION'S SORT ORDER. Because none of the options say
  what we mean. `tee-past` is filled by tag, and the only date Shopify can sort
  it by is when the PRODUCT was created — which is when the tee entered the
  catalogue, months before it held the slot, and in no relation to the week it
  ran. Manual order would work exactly until the agent adds the next one
  unattended. The week number is the real key and it lives in `tee.week`.

  WHY THE STRING DANCE. Liquid's `sort` filter takes a direct property name and
  cannot reach `metafields.tee.week.value`, and Liquid has no way to push onto an
  array. The supported idiom is to build one delimited string, sort that, and
  look the products back up by handle — the week is zero-padded to four digits so
  a plain lexical sort orders 0002 before 0010, which a bare number would not.

  A TEE WITH NO WEEK NUMBER SORTS TO THE BOTTOM rather than the top. An absent
  metafield reads 0, and 0000 sorts first ascending — which would put a
  mis-tagged product at the head of the binder as week 001. Missing numbers get
  9998 instead so they trail the real ones, and the per-card fallback below still
  gives them a plausible number to print.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pairs = ''
  for product in archive.products
    assign wk = product.metafields.tee.week.value | plus: 0
    if wk == 0
      assign wk = 9998
    endif
    assign key = wk | prepend: '000' | slice: -4, 4
    assign pairs = pairs | append: key | append: '~' | append: product.handle | append: ','
  endfor

  assign ordered = pairs | split: ',' | sort
  unless s.order == 'oldest'
    assign ordered = ordered | reverse
  endunless
-%}

<div
  class="aj-teeb color-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
  style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="aj-teeb__inner page-width">
    <header class="aj-teeb__head">
      {%- if s.kicker != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-teeb__kicker">{{ s.kicker | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="aj-teeb__heading">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="aj-teeb__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- if s.body != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-teeb__body">{{ s.body | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The count is rendered rather than written, so it can never be a stale
        number somebody typed once.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="aj-teeb__count">
        <span class="aj-teeb__count-n">{{ filled }}</span>
        {% if filled == 1 %}{{ s.count_one | escape }}{% else %}{{ s.count_many | escape }}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </header>

    {%- if filled > 0 -%}
      <ul class="aj-teeb__grid" role="list">
        {%- for entry in ordered -%}
          {%- liquid
            # Each entry is `0003~some-handle`, built above. The handle is the
            # second half; look the product back up by it.
            #
            # NOT `all_products[handle]`, which is capped at twenty lookups per
            # template — the binder passes twenty in its fifth month and the
            # twenty-first card would simply stop rendering, with nothing said.
            # `where` searches the collection we already have in hand.
            assign handle = entry | split: '~' | last
            assign product = archive.products | where: 'handle', handle | first
          -%}
          {%- if product == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

            # The number the card actually ran as. `| plus: 0` forces the
            # metafield to a number so the zero test below is not comparing a
            # string; an absent metafield yields 0 and falls through.
            assign wk = product.metafields.tee.week.value | plus: 0
            if wk == 0
              # No stored number, so guess from position — which depends on
              # which way round the binder is reading.
              if s.order == 'oldest'
                assign wk = forloop.index
              else
                assign wk = filled | minus: forloop.index0
              endif
            endif

            assign wk_label = wk | append: ''
            if wk < 100
              assign wk_label = wk_label | prepend: '0'
            endif
            if wk < 10
              assign wk_label = wk_label | prepend: '0'
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="aj-teeb__pocket">
            <a class="aj-teeb__slab" href="{{ product.url }}">
              <span class="aj-teeb__glass" aria-hidden="true"></span>

              <span class="aj-teeb__label">
                <span class="aj-teeb__label-set">{{ s.card_series | escape }}</span>
                <span class="aj-teeb__label-no">{{ wk_label }}</span>
              </span>

              <span class="aj-teeb__card">
                <span class="aj-teeb__bands" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="aj-teeb__cardin">
                  <span class="aj-teeb__window">
                    {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
                      {{
                        product.featured_image
                        | image_url: width: 500
                        | image_tag:
                          loading: 'lazy',
                          widths: '200, 320, 500',
                          sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 22vw, (min-width: 750px) 30vw, 44vw',
                          class: 'aj-teeb__art',
                          alt: product.title
                      }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="aj-teeb__plate">
                    <span class="aj-teeb__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</span>
                    {%- comment -%}
                      The archive shows TODAY's price, not the week's price. The
                      discount was restored when the tee left the slot, so
                      printing what it cost that week would be advertising a
                      price nobody can now pay.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span class="aj-teeb__price">
                      {%- if product.available -%}
                        {{ v.price | money }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{ s.gone_label | escape }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The pockets still to fill. `aria-hidden` because "empty slot" repeated
          three times is noise to a screen reader — the count above already says
          how many cards exist.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for i in (1..s.empty_slots) -%}
          <li class="aj-teeb__pocket aj-teeb__pocket--empty" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="aj-teeb__empty">
              <span class="aj-teeb__empty-q">?</span>
              <span class="aj-teeb__empty-t">{{ s.empty_label | escape }}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="aj-teeb__none">{{ s.empty_state | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    The same purple ground as the homepage section, because this page is that
    section's other half and a different colour would break the connection the
    week number is trying to make.
  */
  .aj-teeb {
    --aj-teeb-cream: #f2ead9;
    --aj-teeb-cream-2: #e4d8c0;
    background: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .aj-teeb__inner {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* ---- the header --------------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teeb__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-block-end: 2.5rem;
  }

  .aj-teeb__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-teeb__heading {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 8vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Ink stands in for purple — on this ground the brand purple is a hole. */
  .aj-teeb__rule {
    display: block;
    width: 8rem;
    height: 5px;
    margin: 0 auto 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8) 0 25%,
      var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000) 25% 50%,
      var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828) 50% 75%,
      var(--aj-brand-teal, #30aac6) 75% 100%
    );
  }

  .aj-teeb__body {
    margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    max-width: 46ch;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.86);
  }

  .aj-teeb__count {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.7);
  }

  /*
    The one number on the page, so it gets display size. Flashy's digits are
    narrow — at 1.5rem a single digit beside spaced uppercase read as a stray
    mark rather than as a count.
  */
  .aj-teeb__count-n {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    vertical-align: -0.16em;
    margin-inline-end: 0.35rem;
  }

  /* ---- the binder --------------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teeb__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teeb__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .aj-teeb__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  /*
    EVERY CARD LEANS SLIGHTLY DIFFERENTLY. A grid of perfectly square rectangles
    reads as a spreadsheet; three repeating angles read as objects somebody put
    in pockets by hand. Three is enough — the eye stops looking for the pattern
    past about that, and more would need a rule per card.
  */
  .aj-teeb__pocket:nth-child(3n + 1) .aj-teeb__slab { rotate: -1.6deg; }
  .aj-teeb__pocket:nth-child(3n + 2) .aj-teeb__slab { rotate: 1.1deg; }
  .aj-teeb__pocket:nth-child(3n + 3) .aj-teeb__slab { rotate: -0.5deg; }

  .aj-teeb__slab {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.32), rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1));
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.45);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.65),
      inset 0 -1px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.16),
      0 12px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.34);
    transition: translate 0.2s ease, scale 0.2s ease, rotate 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  /*
    Straightens and lifts, exactly as the homepage slab does. Pulling a card out
    of a pocket is the gesture; whichever card you reach for is the one that
    comes up straight.
  */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-teeb__slab:hover {
      translate: 0 -6px;
      scale: 1.03;
      rotate: 0deg;
      box-shadow:
        inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.8),
        inset 0 -1px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.18),
        0 20px 38px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.46);
    }
  }

  .aj-teeb__slab:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    outline-offset: 3px;
    rotate: 0deg;
  }

  .aj-teeb__glass {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 3;
    pointer-events: none;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      118deg,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 36%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.15) 46%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 58%
    );
  }

  /* The grading label, reduced to the two things legible at this size. */
  .aj-teeb__label {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.28rem 0.4rem;
    margin-block-end: 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--aj-teeb-cream, #f2ead9);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  }

  .aj-teeb__label-set {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.65;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aj-teeb__label-no {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 0.9;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aj-teeb__card {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.28rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--aj-teeb-cream, #f2ead9), var(--aj-teeb-cream-2, #e4d8c0));
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.16);
  }

  .aj-teeb__bands {
    display: block;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8) 0 25%,
      var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000) 25% 50%,
      var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0) 50% 75%,
      var(--aj-brand-teal, #30aac6) 75% 100%
    );
  }

  .aj-teeb__cardin {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-block-start: 0.28rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .aj-teeb__window {
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
  }

  /*
    Cover, matching the homepage card's photo mode. Most of this catalogue's tee
    photography is flat-lay on concrete, which crops to a frame the way card
    photography does.
  */
  .aj-teeb__art {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .aj-teeb__plate {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.45rem 0.35rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    color: var(--aj-teeb-cream, #f2ead9);
  }

  /*
    Two lines and then a clamp. These titles run long — "03 Resident Evil
    Outbreak Ps2 Black T-Shirt" — and a plate that grows to fit breaks the grid
    into ragged rows.
  */
  .aj-teeb__name {
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.12;
  }

  .aj-teeb__price {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: 0.2rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  /* ---- the empty pockets --------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    A dashed outline rather than a card. It has to read as an absence — a pocket
    with nothing in it — and anything with a fill reads as a card that failed to
    load.
  */
  .aj-teeb__pocket--empty .aj-teeb__empty {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 12rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 2px dashed rgb(255 255 255 / 0.32);
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .aj-teeb__empty-q {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.4);
  }

  .aj-teeb__empty-t {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.5);
  }

  .aj-teeb__none {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.8);
  }

  /* ---- motion -------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    Scroll-driven, so no JavaScript. Guarded twice, as everywhere else in this
    theme: @supports for browsers with no view timeline, which see the finished
    state, and reduced-motion for people who asked not to have it.

    The animation owns `translate` and `opacity`; the resting lean owns `rotate`
    and the hover owns `scale`. Three independent properties, so a card that has
    finished animating can still be picked up.
  */
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .aj-teeb__slab {
        animation: aj-teeb-in linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 0% cover 24%;
      }

      @keyframes aj-teeb-in {
        from {
          opacity: 0;
          translate: 0 20px;
        }

        to {
          opacity: 1;
          translate: 0 0;
        }
      }
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Tee archive",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The binder of past Tee of the Week picks. The agent tags each tee 'tee-past' when it leaves the slot and records the week it ran, so this fills itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "archive_handle",
      "label": "Collection handle",
      "info": "The agent maintains 'tee-past'. Change only if that collection is renamed.",
      "default": "tee-past"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "order",
      "label": "Order",
      "info": "Sorted by the week each tee actually ran, not by the collection's own sort order — which is alphabetical and put the numbers out of sequence.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "newest", "label": "Newest week first" },
        { "value": "oldest", "label": "Week 001 first" }
      ],
      "default": "newest"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "The set" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Every tee that made the cut" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "One graphic tee gets sealed up every week. This is all of them, in order, with the week each one ran."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_one", "label": "Count label, singular", "default": "card in the set" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_many", "label": "Count label, plural", "default": "cards in the set" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "gone_label", "label": "Sold-out label", "default": "Sold out" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "empty_state",
      "label": "Text when the set is empty",
      "default": "The first card goes in this week. Come back and watch it fill up."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Card" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "card_series", "label": "Label set name", "default": "The Yoink" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "empty_slots",
      "label": "Empty pockets shown",
      "info": "Blank slots after the last card, so the set reads as unfinished.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 64 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 72 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Tee archive" }]
}
{% endschema %}
